# Repo-root ignores.
#
# fluid-web/ has its own .gitignore covering the Next.js app, but it only
# applies from that directory down — the repo root had no ignore file at all,
# so in a fresh clone nothing here was protected. Most importantly that
# includes env files: the rule existed only as an uncommitted local file, so
# it guarded this working copy and nobody else's.

# Local environment + platform config. Never commit real values —
# fluid-web/.env.example documents the variable names instead.
.env*
!.env.example
.vercel

# macOS directory metadata. Also stops a stray .DS_Store being swept into a
# commit by a broad `git add`.
.DS_Store

# Machine-specific editor / tooling config (e.g. local dev-server paths).
.claude/
